<title>USA: Integra artificial skin gets further okay.</title>
<headline>Integra artificial skin gets further okay.</headline>
<dateline>PLAINSBORO, N.J. 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integra LifeSciences Corp said on Thursday the Center for Devices and Radiological Health of the Food and Drug Administration had approved the company's premarket approval application supplement to manufacture Integra Artificial Skin in sheets of four inches by five inches and eight inches by 10 inches.</p>
<p>In March the FDA approved Integra Artificial Skin for the commercial market in sheets of four inches by 10 inches, Integra said.</p>
</text>
